cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Higgins Decomposition
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Peter
    family-names: Higgins
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Markham, Ontario, Canada
    email: PeterHiggins@RogueWaveAudio.com
repository-code: https://github.com/PeterHiggins19/higgins-decomposition
url: https://peterhiggins19.github.io/higgins-decomposition/
abstract: >-
  Higgins Decomposition (Hˢ) is a deterministic compositional inference
  instrument on the Aitchison simplex. The canonical engine pair is
  CNT (Compositional Navigation Tensor) v3.1.0 and CNQ (Compositional
  Navigation Quaternion) v2.0.0, both with Python and R implementations
  and engine-independent deterministic hash chains. Validated across 11
  domains and 101 reference datasets, plus a 9-country EMBER 2001-2025
  energy-mix corpus for CoDaWork 2026 (Coimbra, June 2026).
keywords:
  - compositional data analysis
  - simplex
  - Aitchison geometry
  - entropy
  - decomposition
  - information theory
  - log-ratio
  - quaternion
license: Apache-2.0
version: 3.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-10"
